      "value": "Likely a UART baud-rate divisor register or clock-divider configuration latch",
      "explanation": "Module has a single 8-bit data input (DataIn) and a single 16-bit data output (DIV), with no event, control, or reset ports. This narrow interface suggests a register that captures an 8-bit value and expands or holds it as a 16-bit divisor value for UART baud-rate generation. The absence of event inputs or control signals implies the module is purely combinational or a simple latch, with data capture controlled externally.",
